contest2026_295_suanliheidong/logs/foamzzz/2026-08-10/codex__019fe9f4-0cc1-7022-ac65-6d3a95946af1.jsonl:1:{"schema_version":"1.0","session_id":"019fe9f4-0cc1-7022-ac65-6d3a95946af1","team_id":"contest2026_295_suanliheidong","github_login":"foamzzz","tool":"codex","seq":1,"ts":"2026-08-10T04:36:51.018Z","role":"user","text":"请先阅读：\n\ncontest2026_295_suanliheidong/board/checkpoints/\nminimal_n16r8_nsh_boot/CODEX_HANDOFF.md\n\n以及：\n\ncontest2026_295_suanliheidong/docs/hardware_work.md\n\n把 CODEX_HANDOFF.md 视为已经验证过的项目背景，不要重新回溯旧问题。\n\n读取完成后检查当前 git status/branch，然后从 Minimal NSH known-good baseline 继续 Stage 2 Peripheral Bring-up。\n\n除非 handoff 与当前仓库实际状态冲突，否则不要重新调查 HAL、esptool、Simple Boot 和 Minimal NSH 启动历史。\n我们已经冻结并备份了一个已验证成功的基线：\n\nESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 Minimal NSH Boot\n\n当前基线已经确认：\n- N16R8 PASS\n- Flash 16MB PASS\n- PSRAM 8MB Octal configured\n- UART0 TX43 / RX44 PASS\n- NSH PASS\n- -j8 build PASS\n- nuttx.bin PASS\n- hardware boot -> nsh> PASS\n\n现在进入下一阶段：\n\nStage 2: Peripheral Bring-up\n\n注意：\n本阶段不是实现产品功能。\n本阶段目标仅仅是把 hardware_work.md 中已经确定的硬件外设正确适配到 NuttX board 层。\n\n==================================================\n0. 工作方式\n==================================================\n\n工作区：\n\n~/vela/openvela\n\nPython/esptool 操作必须：\n\ncd ~/vela/openvela\nsource myenv/bin/activate\n\n继续保留现有：\n\ncontest2026_295_suanliheidong/board/contest_board/\n\n以及：\n- HAL backport 机制\n- build_with_hal_backport.sh\n- esp_hal_lock_backport.sh\n- esptool --use_segments 修复\n- --ram-only-header\n- Simple Boot\n- -j8\n\n不要破坏已经验证成功的 Minimal NSH boot。\n\n如果当前还位于 checkpoint/minimal-n16r8-nsh 分支，\n请从该 checkpoint 创建新的开发分支，例如：\n\nfeature/peripheral-bringup\n\n不要在 checkpoint 分支继续开发。\n\n不要 push，除非我明确要求。\n\n==================================================\n1. 修改边界\n==================================================\n\n长期源码修改只允许：\n\ncontest2026_295_suanliheidong/board/contest_board/**\n\n保持现有 board 映射/构建机制。\n\n禁止直接修改 tracked source：\n\nnuttx/**\nvendor/**\npackages/**\nHAL/**\n\n可以阅读、grep、对比这些源码，\n但不能为了让功能工作而直接修改它们。\n\n如果发现当前 NuttX ESP32-S3 driver 不支持某个需求：\n先报告 blocker，\n不要擅自 patch arch/HAL/NuttX。\n\n==================================================\n2. 先自己调查，不要向我逐项提问\n==================================================\n\n首先读取：\n\nhardware_work.md\n\n然后重点调查当前本地源码：\n\nnuttx/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/\nnuttx/arch/xtensa/src/esp32s3/\nnuttx/drivers/\n\n优先参考：\n\nesp32s3-devkit\nesp32s3-box\nesp32s3-eye\nesp32s3-korvo-2\n\n参考原则：\n\ndevkit:\n基础 GPIO / I2C / PWM / bringup / defconfig\n\nbox:\nbuttons / GPIO / bringup\n\neye:\nGPIO / button / peripheral board structure\n\nkorvo-2:\nI2S / audio / I2C 相关 board adaptation\n\n不要整块复制参考板。\n\n只提取当前 openvela/NuttX 版本已经存在的标准接口和初始化模式。\n\n不要根据记忆猜 API 名。\n所有 API、CONFIG、函数名必须先 grep 当前源码确认。\n\n减少聊天输出：\n调查过程中不要长篇向我解释。\n自行完成调查。\n只有真正遇到无法绕过的 blocker 才停止。\n\n==================================================\n3. 本板硬件定义\n==================================================\n\n保持以下 GPIO 映射为唯一事实来源：\n\nLED:\nGPIO4\nLED_GPIO_PIN\nGPIO output\nboot initial level = LOW\n\n注意：\nhardware_work.md 没有证明 LED 是 active-high 还是 active-low。\n不要自行假设 LED 点亮逻辑。\n当前只要求 GPIO output 初始化。\n\n--------------------------------\n\nMIC I2S:\n\nBCLK/SCK = GPIO16\nWS/LRCK  = GPIO17\nDIN      = GPIO18\n\n方向：\n\nGPIO16 -> output\nGPIO17 -> output\nGPIO18 -> input\n\n--------------------------------\n\nServo PWM:\n\nRIGHT_FRONT  = GPIO9\nRIGHT_REAR   = GPIO10\nLEFT_REAR    = GPIO21\nLEFT_FRONT   = GPIO47\nTAIL         = GPIO48\n\n全部：\n\nLEDC / PWM\n50Hz\n\n本阶段禁止让舵机动作。\n\n初始化要求：\n- 注册 PWM resources\n- 默认不输出危险脉宽\n- 不自动移动舵机\n- bringup 后保持安全 idle/disabled 状态\n\n--------------------------------\n\nOLED I2C:\n\nI2C0\n\nSDA = GPIO12\nSCL = GPIO13\nfrequency = 400000\n\nSDA 需要按当前 ESP32-S3 NuttX I2C 驱动方式配置。\n\n注意：\n\n当前 hardware_work.md 没有 OLED controller 型号和 I2C address。\n\n因此本阶段：\n\nYES:\nI2C0 board adaptation\nI2C bus initialization\n可选注册标准 /dev/i2cX（如果当前 NuttX 架构如此实现）\n\nNO:\nSSD1306/SH1106 等具体 OLED driver\nOLED framebuffer\ngraphics\nLVGL\nOLED application\n\n不要猜 OLED 芯片型号。\n\n--------------------------------\n\nTOUCH_BUTTON:\n\nGPIO14\nGPIO input\n\n虽然宏名叫 TOUCH_BUTTON_GPIO，\n当前 hardware_work.md 描述的是普通 GPIO input/button。\n\n本阶段按 GPIO/button 适配。\n\n不要启用 ESP capacitive-touch driver，\n除非本地硬件资料明确证明这是电容触摸外设。\n\n--------------------------------\n\nBOOT_BUTTON:\n\nGPIO0\nGPIO input\n\nGPIO0 是 boot strap。\n\n要求：\n- 正常启动后才作为 button 使用\n- 不驱动 GPIO0\n- 不配置会破坏正常 SPI Boot 的下拉状态\n- 保持 boot 行为安全\n- README 标记：复位时按住可能进入 ROM download mode\n\n--------------------------------\n\nSpeaker I2S:\n\nLRCK/WS = GPIO38\nBCLK    = GPIO39\nDOUT    = GPIO40\n\n全部 ESP32-S3 -> external device。\n\n当前 hardware_work.md 没有给出具体 amplifier/codec 型号。\n\n因此本阶段只适配 I2S TX。\n\n不要添加：\n- ES8311\n- MAX98357\n- codec driver\n- audio player\n\n除非项目现有硬件资料明确给出具体芯片。\n\n==================================================\n4. Stage 2 要实现的五个 board resource\n==================================================\n\n按下面顺序实施。\n\n------------------------------\nStage 2A - GPIO\n------------------------------\n\n实现：\n\nGPIO4 LED output\nGPIO14 button input\nGPIO0 boot button input\n\n优先使用 NuttX 标准 board API。\n\n调查并参考当前 ESP32-S3 board 的：\n\nboard_userled_initialize\nboard_userled\nboard_userled_all\n\n以及：\n\nboard_button_initialize\nboard_buttons\nboard_button_irq\n\n具体是否采用这些函数，\n必须由当前源码和 CONFIG 决定。\n\n不要为了 API 统一修改 NuttX。\n\n验收：\n- 编译 PASS\n- NSH PASS\n- 不影响 GPIO0 boot\n- 不需要实现 LED 闪烁应用\n- 不需要实现按钮业务 callback\n\n------------------------------\nStage 2B - I2C0\n------------------------------\n\n适配：\n\nGPIO12 SDA\nGPIO13 SCL\n400kHz target\n\n使用当前 ESP32-S3 NuttX I2C driver。\n\n参考本地 board 实现。\n\n目标：\n让 I2C controller 正确初始化/注册。\n\n如果标准工具存在，\n未来可以从 NSH /dev/i2cX 看到设备。\n\n当前不需要 OLED driver。\n\n不要把 GPIO12/13 硬编码到 arch driver。\n引脚配置应该沿用当前 ESP32-S3 Kconfig/board configuration 机制。\n\n------------------------------\nStage 2C - PWM / LEDC\n------------------------------\n\n适配 5 路：\n\nGPIO9\nGPIO10\nGPIO21\nGPIO47\nGPIO48\n\n目标频率：\n\n50Hz\n\n先调查：\n\nESP32-S3 LEDC lower-half\nNuttX PWM upper-half\nCONFIG_PWM\nCONFIG_PWM_MULTICHAN\nESP32S3 PWM/LEDC CONFIG\n\n确认当前版本真正支持的 channel/register 模式。\n\n优先：\n共享 50Hz timer + 5 个独立 LEDC channel。\n\n但不要绕过当前 NuttX driver architecture。\n\n本阶段只需要：\n- PWM lower-half 初始化\n- board register\n- /dev/pwm* 或当前标准接口可用\n- 五个 GPIO 映射正确\n\n禁止：\n- 自动输出 servo angle\n- 自动输出 1ms/1.5ms/2ms pulse\n- 开机让舵机运动\n\n如果注册设备必须产生 PWM：\n默认 duty=0 / disabled，选择当前驱动支持的最安全状态。\n\n------------------------------\nStage 2D - I2S microphone\n------------------------------\n\nMIC：\n\nBCLK GPIO16\nWS   GPIO17\nDIN  GPIO18\n\n目标：\n适配 ESP32-S3 I2S RX resource。\n\n只初始化/register I2S lower-half。\n\n不录音。\n不保存 PCM。\n不做语音识别。\n不启用业务 audio framework。\n\n不要猜：\nsample rate\nbits per sample\nchannel format\nmic chip\n\n如果 NuttX register 阶段必须具有默认格式，\n采用参考 board 的安全默认值，并在 README 标成：\ntemporary/default, not hardware-validated。\n\n------------------------------\nStage 2E - I2S speaker\n------------------------------\n\nSpeaker：\n\nWS   GPIO38\nBCLK GPIO39\nDOUT GPIO40\n\n目标：\n适配 I2S TX resource。\n\n因为 MIC 和 Speaker 使用不同的 BCLK/WS pin group，\n优先调查使用 ESP32-S3 两个独立 I2S controller。\n\n不要未经调查把两套 pin 强塞到一个 controller。\n\n根据本地 NuttX driver/reference board 决定：\n\nI2S0 = MIC / I2S1 = SPK\n\n或\n\nI2S1 = MIC / I2S0 = SPK\n\n选择之后在 README 明确记录。\n\n本阶段：\n不播放声音。\n不增加 codec。\n不增加 audio app。\n\n==================================================\n5. bringup 结构\n==================================================\n\n整理 contest_board/src，使职责清晰。\n\n建议逻辑形式：\n\nboard_bringup\n    |\n    +-- GPIO/button\n    +-…95464 tokens truncated…s checkpoint.\\n+\\n+# Git / Checkpoint\\n+\\n+- Checkpoint path: `board/checkpoints/minimal_n16r8_nsh_boot`\\n+- Checkpoint branch: `checkpoint/minimal-n16r8-nsh`\\n+- Contest HEAD: `d31d5e6c9897b639d8b78d271149a7b6bec41f34`\\n+- NuttX HEAD: `76354c637858ecb0aa4601629327acb6f44a26bb`\\n+- HAL HEAD: `9fc713a95b1ff150dd0b0647e465d3c624056bb1`\\n+- Recommended future branch: `feature/peripheral-bringup`\\n+\\n+Do not create that future branch as part of this handoff.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","output":null,"is_error":false}
contest2026_295_suanliheidong/logs/foamzzz/2026-08-08/codex__019fe116-ca59-7841-a4a0-0f954a738fdd.jsonl:885:{"schema_version":"1.0","session_id":"019fe116-ca59-7841-a4a0-0f954a738fdd","team_id":"contest2026_295_suanliheidong","github_login":"foamzzz","tool":"codex","seq":769,"ts":"2026-08-10T04:28:11.840Z","role":"tool","tool_name":"exec","tool_call_id":"call_Jd5WxTyQGZlDTsDs3shMeaFb","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: contest2026_295_suanliheidong/board/checkpoints/minimal_n16r8_nsh_boot/CODEX_HANDOFF.md\\n+# Project\\n+\\n+Workspace: `~/vela/openvela`\\n+\\n+Contest repo: `~/vela/openvela/contest2026_295_suanliheidong`\\n+\\n+GitHub repository: `https://github.com/foamzzz/contest2026_295_suanliheidong.git`\\n+\\n+Current branch and checkpoint branch: `checkpoint/minimal-n16r8-nsh`\\n+\\n+Contest HEAD: `d31d5e6c9897b639d8b78d271149a7b6bec41f34`\\n+\\n+Remotes: `origin` is the GitHub repository; `openvela` is the Gitee remote\\n+`git@gitee.com:open-vela/contest2026_295_suanliheidong`.\\n+\\n+The manifest maps `board/contest_board` to the symlinked\\n+`vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_295_board`; do not maintain a second copy.\\n+\\n+# Hardware\\n+\\n+Module: ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8\\n+\\n+- Flash: 16MB\\n+- PSRAM: 8MB Octal / OPI\\n+- UART0 TX: GPIO43\\n+- UART0 RX: GPIO44\\n+- UART0 baud: 115200\\n+\\n+Hardware is verified through ROM boot → NuttX boot → NSH:\\n+`*** Booting NuttX ***`, `NuttShell (NSH)`, `nsh>`.\\n+\\n+# Minimal Baseline Status\\n+\\n+- N16R8: PASS\\n+- Flash 16MB: PASS\\n+- PSRAM 8MB Octal: CONFIGURED; runtime stress test NOT FULLY RUNTIME VERIFIED\\n+- UART0 + NSH: PASS\\n+- `-j8` build: PASS\\n+- `nuttx.bin`: PASS\\n+- Hardware boot: PASS\\n+- Wi-Fi / Bluetooth / LCD / Camera / Audio: DISABLED\\n+\\n+# Current NSH Runtime\\n+\\n+Verified on hardware: `help`, `uname -a`, `ls /dev`, `echo`, and UART0 I/O.\\n+`/dev` includes `console`, `ttyS0`, `null`, and `zero`.\\n+\\n+`free` and `ps` are NOT ENABLED. Their `command not found` result is expected\\n+for this minimal configuration, not a boot failure.\\n+\\n+# Python Environment\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+cd ~/vela/openvela\\n+if [ ! -d myenv ]; then python3 -m venv myenv; fi\\n+source myenv/bin/activate\\n+python --version\\n+python -m esptool version\\n+```\\n+\\n+Validated esptool: `v5.3.1`. Do not use `/home/foam/.local/bin/esptool.py`.\\n+\\n+# Correct Build Procedure\\n+\\n+Use the wrapper, not ordinary `build.sh` directly:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+cd ~/vela/openvela\\n+source myenv/bin/activate\\n+contest2026_295_suanliheidong/board/contest_board/scripts/build_with_hal_backport.sh -j8\\n+```\\n+\\n+For a log:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+set -o pipefail\\n+contest2026_295_suanliheidong/board/contest_board/scripts/build_with_hal_backport.sh \\\\\\n+  -j8 2>&1 | tee ~/contest-board-build.log\\n+```\\n+\\n+The wrapper activates `myenv`, verifies/applies the HAL backport, builds the\\n+custom board, and reverts the patch on success or failure.\\n+\\n+Artifacts: `nuttx/nuttx` (ELF), `nuttx/nuttx.bin` (flash image),\\n+`nuttx/nuttx.hex` (Intel HEX).\\n+\\n+# HAL Compatibility Backport\\n+\\n+HAL base: `9fc713a95b1ff150dd0b0647e465d3c624056bb1`\\n+\\n+Upstream fix: `454d82c70ed`, `Change lock constant defines with SP macro`.\\n+\\n+Affected files: `components/esp_hw_support/clk_ctrl_os.c` and\\n+`components/esp_hw_support/modem_clock.c`. They define\\n+`LOCK_INITIALIZER_UNLOCKED 0`, incompatible with the current NuttX\\n+`spinlock_t`; the backport changes it to `SP_UNLOCKED`.\\n+\\n+Board-local mechanism:\\n+\\n+- `board/contest_board/patches/0001-esp-hal-nuttx-lock-initializer.patch`\\n+- `board/contest_board/scripts/esp_hal_lock_backport.sh`\\n+- `board/contest_board/scripts/build_with_hal_backport.sh`\\n+\\n+Flow: verify base → temporary apply → build → automatic revert → HAL clean.\\n+Do not upgrade the whole HAL: newer layouts do not match current NuttX\\n+`hal.mk`. Do not directly modify HAL tracked source.\\n+\\n+**DO NOT REMOVE WITHOUT A VALID UPSTREAM-COMPATIBLE SOLUTION.**\\n+\\n+# Critical esptool Fix\\n+\\n+The former wrapper injected `--use_segments` / `--use-segments` into\\n+`elf2image`. Esptool then treated ELF Program Header PhysAddr values\\n+`0x20`, `0x10000`, and `0x20000` as ROM load addresses, causing\\n+`StoreProhibited` with `EXCVADDR=0x00000020`.\\n+\\n+Current `scripts/esptool.py` injects neither flag. It runs\\n+`sys.executable -m esptool` from the active virtualenv and preserves\\n+`--ram-only-header`. **NEVER REINTRODUCE `--use_segments` FOR THIS IMAGE FLOW.**\\n+\\n+# Boot Image Model\\n+\\n+NuttX Simple Boot, one image: `nuttx.bin`; flash offset `0x000000`;\\n+Flash 16MB, DIO, 40m. Do not add ESP-IDF `bootloader.bin`, partition table,\\n+or OTA data.\\n+\\n+# Image Validation\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+cd ~/vela/openvela\\n+source myenv/bin/activate\\n+python -m esptool --chip esp32s3 image-info nuttx/nuttx.bin\\n+```\\n+\\n+Validated: Entry `0x40374f2c`; DRAM segment `0x3fc8b840`; IRAM segment\\n+`0x40374000`; Flash 16MB/DIO/40m; checksum valid. Valid RAM segments must be\\n+`0x3fc...` or `0x403...`; reject `0x00000020` as a ROM load segment.\\n+\\n+# Flash Procedure\\n+\\n+Only after image-info passes:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+cd ~/vela/openvela\\n+source myenv/bin/activate\\n+python -m esptool --chip esp32s3 --port /dev/ttyUSB0 --baud 460800 \\\\\\n+  write-flash --flash-size 16MB --flash-mode dio --flash-freq 40m \\\\\\n+  0x000000 nuttx/nuttx.bin\\n+```\\n+\\n+# UART Wiring\\n+\\n+- USB-TTL RXD → GPIO43\\n+- USB-TTL TXD → GPIO44\\n+- USB-TTL GND → board GND\\n+- Do not connect USB-TTL 3V3/5V to the board.\\n+- Use an independent stable 5V supply.\\n+\\n+USB-TTL board power previously caused `BROWNOUT_RST`; do not restore it.\\n+\\n+# Known Non-blocking Boot Message\\n+\\n+Simple Boot may print `SHA-256 comparison failed` and `Attempting to boot\\n+anyway...`; hardware then reaches NuttX and `nsh>`. Treat this as non-blocking\\n+for this baseline; do not add an ESP-IDF bootloader to suppress it.\\n+\\n+# Modification Boundaries\\n+\\n+Long-term board maintenance is limited to:\\n+`contest2026_295_suanliheidong/board/contest_board/**`.\\n+\\n+Do not directly maintain tracked changes in `nuttx/**`, `vendor/**`,\\n+`packages/**`, or HAL. Read them for reference only; do not patch arch/HAL for\\n+quick compilation.\\n+\\n+# Important Board-specific Change\\n+\\n+`src/board_bringup.c` returns `0` on success. Do not change it to `return OK;`\\n+unless a verified header supplies `OK` and the change is necessary.\\n+\\n+# Minimal Baseline Files\\n+\\n+- `board/contest_board/README.md` — build and validation guide\\n+- `board/contest_board/configs/nsh/defconfig` — minimal configuration\\n+- `board/contest_board/src/board_boot.c` — empty board hooks\\n+- `board/contest_board/src/board_bringup.c` — successful no-op bring-up\\n+- `board/contest_board/src/board_appinit.c` — optional boardctl hook\\n+- `board/contest_board/src/contest_board.h` — bring-up prototype\\n+- `board/contest_board/patches/0001-esp-hal-nuttx-lock-initializer.patch` — backport\\n+- `board/contest_board/scripts/esp_hal_lock_backport.sh` — apply/revert guard\\n+- `board/contest_board/scripts/build_with_hal_backport.sh` — official build entry\\n+- `board/contest_board/scripts/esptool.py` — active-venv esptool launcher\\n+- `board/contest_board/scripts/Make.defs` — linker/toolchain settings\\n+- `board/contest_board/include/board.h` — board include surface\\n+\\n+# Next Stage\\n+\\n+Stage 2 - Peripheral Bring-up. Read `docs/hardware_work.md` before changes.\\n+Resources to investigate, not implement in this checkpoint:\\n+\\n+- GPIO4 LED; GPIO14 touch/button; GPIO0 boot button\\n+- I2C0: SDA GPIO12, SCL GPIO13, 400kHz\\n+- Servo PWM/LEDC: GPIO9, GPIO10, GPIO21, GPIO47, GPIO48 at 50Hz\\n+- MIC I2S: BCLK GPIO16, WS GPIO17, DIN GPIO18\\n+- Speaker I2S: WS GPIO38, BCLK GPIO39, DOUT GPIO40\\n+\\n+Reference boards: `nuttx/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/esp32s3-devkit`,\\n+`esp32s3-box`, `esp32s3-eye`, and `esp32s3-korvo-2`.\\n+\\n+Prioritize driver/resource/register adaptation. Do not immediately implement\\n+OLED graphics, servo motion, recording, playback, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, or app\\n+logic.\\n+\\n+# Unknown Hardware Details\\n+\\n+`hardware_work.md` does not establish the OLED controller/address, exact\\n+microphone chip, or speaker amplifier/codec. Do not guess SSD1306, SH1106,\\n+INMP441, MAX98357, ES8311, or another part number. Start only with verified\\n+GPIO, I2C, PWM, or I2S resources.\\n+\\n+# New Session Rules\\n+\\n+1. Read this file first, then `docs/hardware_work.md`.\\n+2. Check contest branch and Git status.\\n+3. Treat Minimal NSH as known-good; do not re-investigate HAL, esptool, boot,\\n+   or NSH history unless live facts disagree.\\n+4. Create a new peripheral branch before Stage 2; do not develop directly on\\n+   `checkpoint/minimal-n16r8-nsh`.\\n+5. Do not add features to this checkpoint.\\n+\\n+# Git / Checkpoint\\n+\\n+- Checkpoint: `board/checkpoints/minimal_n16r8_nsh_boot`\\n+- Branch: `checkpoint/minimal-n16r8-nsh`\\n+- Contest HEAD: `d31d5e6c9897b639d8b78d271149a7b6bec41f34`\\n+- NuttX HEAD: `76354c637858ecb0aa4601629327acb6f44a26bb`\\n+- HAL HEAD: `9fc713a95b1ff150dd0b0647e465d3c624056bb1`\\n+- Future branch suggestion: `feature/peripheral-bringup` (do not create here)\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","output":null,"is_error":false}

